Q: Powershell can&#39;t delete file it opened A: <p>Not really sure why aren't you using <code>Compress-Archive</code>, it'd be much simpler:</p>
<pre class="lang-bash prettyprint-override"><code>foreach ($file in $files) {
    try {
        # Create the destination zip path (same folder, same name, .zip extension)
        $zipPath = Join-Path $sourceDir ($file.BaseName + '.ZIP')
        $file | Compress-Archive -DestinationPath $zipPath -ErrorAction Stop
        Write-Host &quot;Zipped '$($file.Name)' to '$zipPath'&quot;

    }
    catch {
        Write-Error &quot;Failed to zip '$($file.Name)': $_&quot;
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>If you're looking for a purely .NET approach, a simplified way is using <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/system.io.compression.zipfile.open" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>ZipFile.Open</code></a> with <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/system.io.compression.ziparchivemode" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>ZipArchiveMode.Create</code></a> to create and open the archive and <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/es-es/dotnet/api/system.io.compression.zipfileextensions.createentryfromfile" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>ZipFileExtensions.CreateEntryFromFile</code></a> to create the archive entries, leaving <code>$archive</code> as the only file handle you need to dispose:</p>
<pre class="lang-bash prettyprint-override"><code>foreach ($file in $files) {
    try {
        # Create the destination zip path (same folder, same name, .zip extension)
        $zipPath = Join-Path $sourceDir ($file.BaseName + '.ZIP')

        # Create and open the archive
        $archive = [System.IO.Compression.ZipFile]::Open(
            $zipPath, [System.IO.Compression.ZipArchiveMode]::Create)

        # Create the entry
        $null = [System.IO.Compression.ZipFileExtensions]::CreateEntryFromFile(
            $archive, $file.FullName, $file.Name)

        Write-Host &quot;Zipped '$($file.Name)' to '$zipPath'&quot;

    }
    catch {
        Write-Error &quot;Failed to zip '$($file.Name)': $_&quot;
    }
    finally {
        if ($archive) { $archive.Dispose() }
    }
}
</code></pre>

