Q: How to declare struct defined in different namespace? A: <p>It's in a global namespace. So when you want to declare:Foo::DeviceAddress the compiler doesn't see the struct in the namespace. What you should do is:</p>
<pre><code> namespace Foo {  
   struct DeviceAddress {  
       uint8_t systemID;         
       uint8_t deviceID;     
       uint8_t componentID;    
   }; 
 } 
</code></pre>
<p>or because you already declared the struct inside Foo:</p>
<pre><code>  namespace Foo {
    struct DeviceAddress;
  } 
  struct Foo::DeviceAddress {
      uint8_t systemID;
      uint8_t deviceID;
      uint8_t componentID;
  };
</code></pre>
